    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469-a2">

                <pb facs="0906" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg782"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    245.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Mariscal to Mr.
                            Morgan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 29,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have received your excellency’s
                    note of the 27th instant, in which, complying with the instructions of your
                    government, you inclosed a copy of a letter addressed to the Secretary of State
                    by the Secretary of War, and a telegram addressed by the adjutant-general of the
                    Department of Texas to the commanding officer at Fort Brown relating to the
                    death of General Servando Canales.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say to your excellency that the President has read with great
                    interest the aforesaid document, and sincerely acknowledges the demonstration
                    made in honor of the deceased General Canales by the military commandant at Fort
                    Brown.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>IGNACIO MARISCAL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
